.planning/phases/01-escalation-mechanism-and-fixture-invariant\01-REVIEWS.md:107:- **MEDIUM — NEWLY RAISED:** The escalated zero-skip acceptance criterion conflicts with mandatory `set -o pipefail`. At `01-03-PLAN.md:412`, the plan requires a filtered pipeline to “print `0`” when there are no skip events. A final `grep -c` prints `0` but exits status 1 when it finds no matches; under `pipefail`, that makes the pipeline fail even though zero skips is the desired result. The automated block at line 407 avoids this particular check, so the acceptance criterion remains unrunnable as written.
